  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manoj R vs Palakkad Municipality on 8 July, 2025 Author: C.S.Dias Bench: C.S.Dias Wp(C) Nos.24796, 24658 & 29545 of 2023 2025:Ker:50276 1 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice C.S.Dias Tuesday, The 8Th Day Of July 2025 / 17Th Ashadha, 1947 Wp(C) No. 24796 Of 2023 Petitioner: Safwan K.E, Aged 34 Years S/O Ibrahim,Kunnappully House,Pazhaya Lakkidi, Akalur P.O.,Palakkad, Pin - 679302 By Advs. Dr.George Abraham Shri.Joby D Joseph",
    "facts": "2. The petitioners in these writ petitions were the successful bidders in the tender floated by the Kerala State Road Transport Corporation (KSRTC) for allotting of spaces within its bus station in Palakkad. Consequently, the petitioners erected temporary sheds within the above property on the Manoj R vs Palakkad Municipality on 8 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/188217403/ 4 strength of the No-objection certificate issued by the KSRTC. They had executed agreements and deposited the requisite amount with the KSRTC. Although the petitioners have submitted applications before the 2 nd respondent, to assign temporary building numbers for their WP(C) Nos.24796, 24658 & 29545 of 2023 2025:KER:50276 sheds, to enable them to apply for license, the applications have not been considered. Subsequently, they have also submitted representations to the 2nd respondent, to assign the temporary numbers. But, the representations have also not been considered till date. In W.P.(C) No. 20664 of 2023, a case of an identical nature, this Court had directed the 2nd respondent to consider applications for temporary building numbers. The petitioners are entitled to the benefit of the said judgment. The learned Standing Counsel appearing for the KSRTC submits that, the petitioners have already instituted civil suits before the jurisdictional Court and orders of temporary injunction have been passed against the KSRTC from evicting the petitioners from the property. Moreover, alleging that the temporary sheds have been unauthorisedly constructed in the property, the 2 nd respondent has refused to issue occupancy certificate to the KSRTC for their building.",
